{"diagnosis": "Trace shows 256-word NOP fetch test ending in TRAP: cpu trap asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead at CYCLES=2009. NOP is ADDI x0,x0,0 with opcode 7'b0010011, but picorv32.v:877 compares is_alu_reg_imm to 7'b0010001 so decode never asserts and CPU traps as illegal. CONE_SLICE is fallback-window (picosoc/picosoc.v:146 cpu instantiation, picosoc/picosoc.v:127 mem_ready) with no decode refs, so trace+excerpt win and root cause is the single-bit opcode typo at picorv32.v:877.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -874,5 +874,5 @@
 			is_beq_bne_blt_bge_bltu_bgeu <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100011;
 			is_lb_lh_lw_lbu_lhu          <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0000011;
 			is_sb_sh_sw                  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0100011;
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010001;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
 			is_alu_reg_reg               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110011;", "expected": "tohost PASS (vs FAIL 0xdead) with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted and fetch progress"}

